# s4-engine-skeleton -> CORE-WIRE-G2

New crate `native/core/crates/mixdog-browser-engine` (all its files are created; no compose call, no protocol row, nothing for
SERVICE_PENDING: the skeleton registers no service).

## native/core/Cargo.toml

- `[workspace] members`, directly after `"crates/mixdog-browser-policy",`:
  `    "crates/mixdog-browser-engine",`
- `[workspace.dependencies]`, directly after the `mixdog-browser-policy = { path = "crates/mixdog-browser-policy" }` line:
  `mixdog-browser-engine = { path = "crates/mixdog-browser-engine" }`

## Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack

- `cargo update --workspace --offline` (the new package's lock entry: its dependencies are mixdog-app-protocol, mixdog-core-api,
  mixdog-protocol, mixdog-rt, mixdog-browser-policy, mixdog-testkit (optional, test-support), async-trait, bytes, serde, serde_json,
  mixdog-workspace-hack; dev: tokio), then `cargo hakari generate` and `cargo hakari manage-deps` (the crate already depends on
  `mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }`).
- Features: `mixdog-browser-engine` has `test-support = ["dep:mixdog-testkit"]`. A replay package of the engine enables it; the
  engine's own tests need no feature (testkit is also a dev-dependency).

## Later wiring (not this wave)

- Nothing in mixdog-tools or the daemon depends on the crate yet; the task that wires the engine into `mixdog-tools` adds
  `mixdog-browser-engine = { workspace = true }` to its Cargo.toml.
